[COMMENTS]
STATION,Site replaced in 1976 by 54007 Arrow at Broom - a crump profile weir with a higher containment capacity. GENERAL: Not rated above bankfull when extensive inundation occurred. Replaced in 1976 by 54007 Arrow at Broom - a crump profile weir with a higher containment capacity. There is a wide floodplain on the right bank (~200m) and a bypass channel on the left bank. STATION HYDROMETRY: Not rated above bankfull when extensive inundation occurred. Less confidence in flows after 1976, following station replacement. Two ratings applied across the period of record, the most recent is valid from October-1973. Bank full pre 1973 2.5mASD and 2mASD. Ratings fit well to respective gaugings. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Groundwater pumping for PWS significantly augments low flow through effluent returns.
CATCHMENT,Low relief, predominantly agricultural catchment upon Keuper Marl, with small glacial gravel deposits in the eastern headwaters. Responsive; sewage effluent maintains low flows. Contains Redditch and Alcester.
Qmed Suitability,Both ratings fit gaugings well to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,No gaugings exist to validate rating beyond QMED.
[END]
